## Opening and Closing Tags 

#### Most HTML elements come in pairs — an opening tag and a closing tag.

- #### The opening tag starts the element (for example, `<p>`).

- #### The closing tag ends it (for example, `</p>`).

- #### The slash / in the closing tag tells the browser that the element is finished.

#### Everything between those two tags is the content that the browser will display.

> 💡 **Tip:** Think of tags like a sandwich: the opening tag is the top bun, the closing tag is the bottom bun, and the content goes in between!

#### ***Remember:*** *it is not important that you know what every tag is. This is an overview to help you grasp the big picture. Take time to look over the HTML code generated by the AI and see what you can recognize or understand.* 

MARKDOWN
